# Calculator
// A pocket calculator:  a number, an operator, another number, and the total as you type.
// Its keys are Spell UI's buttons, four a row, and each one runs one of the calculator's actions.

calculator is an app:
	// The sum being typed:  its left number, its operator and its right number
	- group "what it keeps"
	// The number being typed, as text, so each key can add a digit on the end
	- its "input" is text
	- its "left" is text
	- its "operator" is text
	- its "right" is text
	// The sum so far, worked out each time it's read
	- its "total" is:
		set left number to the left as a number
		set right number to the right as a number
		if the operator is "+" return left number + right number
		if the operator is "–" return left number - right number
		if the operator is "×" return left number times right number
		return left number divided by right number
	// What the display's top line shows:  0 until a key's pressed
	- its "sum" is:
		set shown to "0" if the left is empty otherwise the left
		return shown + " " + the operator + " " + the right
	// The display's second line:  the total, once there's a right number
	- its "output" is:
		"" if the right is empty
		"= " + the total otherwise

	- group "what its keys do"
	- to clear it:
		clear the input
		clear the left
		clear the operator
		clear the right
	// Equals:  the total becomes the left number, ready for the next operator
	- to finish it:
		if the right is empty return
		set the left to the total as text
		clear the operator
		clear the right
		clear the input
	// A digit, or the decimal point:  onto the number being typed, the left one until there's an operator
	- to press (digit as text) on it:
		if the digit is "."
			if the input is empty
				set the input to "0."
			otherwise if the input does not contain "."
				set the input to the input + "."
		otherwise
			set the input to the input + the digit
		if the operator is empty
			set the left to the input
		otherwise
			set the right to the input
	// An operator:  after a whole sum, the total carries on as the next sum's left number
	- to apply (key as text) to it:
		if the right is not empty
			finish it
		set the operator to the key
		clear the input

	- group "drawing"
	// The display, then the keypad, four keys a row:  C and 0 are two keys wide
	- to draw it:
		<ui-stack align="center">
			<ui-card>
				<ui-segment appearance="secondary" align="right">
					<ui-text size="huge">{the sum}</ui-text>
					<ui-space/>
					<ui-text size="large" color="grey">{the output}</ui-text>
				</ui-segment>
				<ui-content>
					<ui-grid columns="4" spacing="compact">
						<ui-column width="8"><ui-button fluid color="negative" onClick={clear it}>C</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid color="secondary" onClick={finish it}>=</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid color="primary" onClick={apply "÷" to it}>÷</ui-button></ui-column>

						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "7" on it}>7</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "8" on it}>8</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "9" on it}>9</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid color="primary" onClick={apply "×" to it}>×</ui-button></ui-column>

						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "4" on it}>4</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "5" on it}>5</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "6" on it}>6</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid color="primary" onClick={apply "–" to it}>–</ui-button></ui-column>

						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "1" on it}>1</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "2" on it}>2</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "3" on it}>3</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid color="primary" onClick={apply "+" to it}>+</ui-button></ui-column>

						<ui-column width="8"><ui-button fluid onClick={press "0" on it}>0</ui-button></ui-column>
						<ui-column><ui-button fluid onClick={press "." on it}>.</ui-button></ui-column>
					</ui-grid>
				</ui-content>
			</ui-card>
		</ui-stack>

	// 12 + 5, then times 2:  the total carries on as the next sum's left number
	- to test two sums in a row:
		press "1" on it
		press "2" on it
		apply "+" to it
		press "5" on it
		its output should be "= 17"
		apply "×" to it
		press "2" on it
		its output should be "= 34"
		finish it
		its left should be "34"
		its output should be ""
